course: dictionary
lesson: 2389
title: The curliness of words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Curliness is a noun, a naming word. It means the quality of being curly, or how much something bends or curls. «Eating crusts does not make hair curly; curliness comes mostly from your genes and the shape of the tiny pocket each hair grows from.» The clues say curliness comes from genes and the shape of the pocket, not from food. So curliness is about how hair is shaped.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it in. «The curliness of her hair» becomes «how curly her hair is», and the sentence still makes sense. That tells you curliness means how curly something is.
explain: Curliness is not only about hair. A pig's tail, a fern or a ribbon can have curliness too. The ending -ness turns the describing word curly into a naming word, the quality of being curly.
fact: Curliness is a noun: it names a quality.
fact: «Curliness» means the quality of being curly, or how much something bends or curls.
fact: «Natural curliness» means curls that you are born with, not curls made by styling.
fact: Curliness often runs in families, because it comes mostly from genes.
fact: Hair is curly partly because of the shape of the hair follicle, the tiny pocket each hair grows from. Oval follicles make curlier hair.
exercise: «The curliness of her hair made it spring back into shape.» What does curliness mean? | How long her hair is | *How curly something is | How fast she runs | The colour of her hair
exercise: Curly is a describing word. What kind of word is curliness? | An adverb, a word that tells how | *A noun, a naming word for a quality | A verb, a doing word | A colour
exercise: «Eating crusts does not make hair curly; curliness comes mostly from your genes.» What mostly causes curliness? | Sunlight in summer | Eating crusts | *Your genes and the shape of the hair follicle | Brushing your hair every day
test: «The fern's natural curliness made each frond look like a spiral.» What does natural curliness mean? | A type of fern food | *Curls and twists a plant is born with | Being very tall | Being wet from rain
test: A pig's tail has great curliness. What does this describe? | *How much the tail bends and curls | Where the pig sleeps | How heavy the pig is | How loud the pig squeals
exam: Which sentence uses curliness correctly? | The curliness ran over the bridge | I curliness the dog yesterday | Curliness is a loud shout | *The curliness of the ribbon made it perfect for the gift
